I look at the clothes on the shelves.
I see a thick sweater.
It is red.
I need a warm sweater.
The shop has many sizes.
I find a size medium.
I walk into the fitting room.
I put the red sweater on.
I have it on and look in the big mirror.
The sweater fits perfectly.
It is incredibly warm.
I love the red colour.
I look at the price tag.
The sweater costs three hundred kroner.
It is a good price for a thick sweater.
I take the sweater off again.
I buy it.
